N2  - Objective: To observe the clinical effect of lumber Du channel electrical acupuncture matching with HANS on lumbar vertebral disc herniation (LDH). Method: One hundred forty patients with LDH were randomly divided into two groups. Electrical acupuncture matching with HANS was used in group one and nerve block in lumbar epidural space was used in group two. Results: The concentration of plasma β-endorphin was increased obviously in group one after the treatment (P < 0.05). But the increase had no significant difference between two groups as well as the results of visual analog scales (VAS) and clinical effect (P > 0.05). Conclusion: Lumber Du channel electrical acupuncture matching with HANS could treat LDH through enhancing the concentration level of β-endorphin. The effect was similar to nerve block in epidural space. It was especially appropriate for patients not suitable receiving epidural space nerve block.
